# Distinguish analyzed audio from inferred Music DNA

- Build independently addressable, versioned profiles linked to source identity and selected current analysis. Never destroy historical analysis.
- Source metadata and third-party reviews do not prove audio-observed instruments, playing technique, bar timing or vocal phrasing.
- Label observations as audio_observed, human_verified, source_inferred/editorial or not_analyzed. Express uncertainty explicitly.
- Record track, artist, release/version, source URL/kind, recording SHA256 when bytes exist, notes, evidence, analyzer version and provenance.
- Extract when grounded: instrument roles, playing technique, tone/timbre, vocals and harmonies, beat/BPM/meter, groove, musical form, harmony, buildup, production and dynamics, emotional arc and optional bar-level observations.
- Do not pretend to hear YouTube/Spotify from a URL alone. Do not bypass streaming DRM or site access and do not reproduce copyrighted lyrics.
- Consult src/music-dna.mjs, src/music-dna-api.mjs and tests before changing format or semantics.
